# HackWatch — Agent Rules

## Critical invariants (never break)

1. `planted_label` must NEVER appear in `MonitorObservation` — monitor cannot see ground truth
2. No exploit primitive may write its own name into generated file content or paths
3. `HackWatchState.to_dict()` excludes `planted_label`; only `to_dict_full()` includes it

## DO NOT

- Do NOT add `planted_label` to `MonitorObservation` (models.py)
- Do NOT set GRPO `beta < 0.01` — collapses KL penalty
- Do NOT remove `calibration_penalty` from reward.py — prevents confidence gaming
- Do NOT remove the `heldout_novel` split from exploits.py — it's the generalization test claim
- Do NOT re-add easy/medium/hard difficulty tiers — dropped by design decision
- Do NOT use `innerHTML` or `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in the demo frontend — agent-generated strings are untrusted

## Python environment

Always use: `/Users/afrasaboobackerp/miniconda3/envs/hackwatch/bin/python`

Run tests: `/Users/afrasaboobackerp/miniconda3/envs/hackwatch/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -v`

## Read first

- `AGENTS.md` — current state, next steps, module map
- `CLAUDE.md` — stack, conda env, invariants
- `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` — architecture overview (if it exists)
